From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:21:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: report radar on the band chanctx

The driver reports a radar with a NULL channel context, which
mac80211 treats as every context on the wiphy. With one wiphy for all
radios, a radar on 5 GHz then cancels CAC and sends radar events for
the 2.4 and 6 GHz channels too, and on a board with two 5 GHz radios
it would mark the DFS channels of the other radio unavailable.

Report the radar on the context of the band that detected it. A radar
that arrives while the band swaps its context for a channel switch
matches no context and is not reported; the detector restarts on the
new channel in that window.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c |   16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -592,9 +592,24 @@ mt7996_mcu_rx_radar_detected(struct mt79
 						&dev->rdd2_chandef,
 						GFP_ATOMIC);
 	} else {
-		phy->rdd_hw_value = chandef->chan->hw_value;
+		struct mt76_chanctx *ctx = READ_ONCE(phy->mt76->chanctx);
+
 		phy->rdd_tx_paused = true;
-		ieee80211_radar_detected(mphy->hw, NULL);
+
+		/* a NULL context flags the contexts of every radio on the
+		 * wiphy, so a band without a context reports nothing
+		 */
+		if (ctx) {
+			phy->rdd_hw_value = chandef->chan->hw_value;
+			ieee80211_radar_detected(mphy->hw,
+						 container_of((void *)ctx,
+							      struct ieee80211_chanctx_conf,
+							      drv_priv));
+		} else {
+			dev_info(dev->mt76.dev,
+				 "%s: no channel context on band %d, radar not reported\n",
+				 __func__, phy->mt76->band_idx);
+		}
 	}
 	dev->hw_pattern++;
 
